adaptive-motion-scaling

This project is derived from Residual Copilot
(https://github.com/shuosha/Residual_Copilot), released under the Apache License 2.0,
by way of huangid/vla-shared-autonomy, which modified and extended it.

Changes from the original include a SpaceMouse teleoperation pilot, additional
block-manipulation tasks, SmolVLA policy integration, shared-autonomy and evaluation
scripts, and the motion-scaling work in this repository.

third_party/lerobot is a git submodule of LeRobot (https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot),
distributed under its own license.

The tube transfer task displays a test tube rack and a test tube from LabUtopia
(Li et al., 2025, "LabUtopia: High-Fidelity Simulation and Hierarchical Benchmark for
Scientific Embodied Agents", https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.22634), published at
https://huggingface.co/datasets/Ruinwalker/LabUtopia-Dataset under CC BY-NC 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/). The files are downloaded at runtime and
are not distributed with this repository. The tube is cut out of LabUtopia's TestTube_02
set, the rack is re-triangulated and shortened from six holes to three (source) and one
(destination), and both models are rescaled to fit the task's colliders.
